battle_script_commands.c: the page's hacks for testing (platform/include/hacks.h).

The EXP a Pokémon gains is multiplied (Cmd_getexp, after the Lucky Egg and the
other bonuses, before the message says it); a ball's catch odds become
certain (Cmd_handleballthrow); a hit's damage becomes enough to knock the
foe out (the adjust*damage commands, after Endure and the Focus Band, before
the HP bar moves). With the hacks off each call gives back what it is given.

And the remake layer learns when a move fails at its foe (JumpIfMoveFailed:
it missed, the foe protected itself, or it has no effect), which no animation
shows: it acts it out.

